ga PR', 'Mirassol', 'Mixto', 'Mogi Mirim', 'Monsoon FC', 'Moto Club de São Luís', 'Moto Clube', 'Murici', 'Nacional AM', 'Nautico Capibaribe', 'Nautico RR', 'Nova Iguacu', 'Nova Mutum', 'Nova Mutum EC', 'Nova Venecia FC', 'Novo Hamburgo', 'Novorizontino', 'Oeste', 'Operario FC MS', 'Operario MS', 'Operario MT', 'Operario PR', 'PSTC', 'Palmas FR', 'Palmeiras', 'Parana', 'Parauapebas', 'Parnahyba', 'Paysandu', 'Penarol AM', 'Picos', 'Ponte Preta', 'Porto Velho EC', 'Portuguesa Desportos', 'Portuguesa RJ', 'Pouso Alegre', 'Princesa do Solimoes', 'Real Ariquemes', 'Real FC', 'Real Noroeste', 'Real Noroeste ES', 'Red Bull Brasil', 'Remo', 'Remo PA', 'Resende', 'Resende RJ', 'Retro', 'Retro FC Brasil', 'Rio Branco AC', 'Rio Branco ES', 'River (PI)', 'River AC', 'SC Genus', 'SE Gama', 'Salgueiro', 'Sampaio Correa', 'Santa Cruz FC', 'Santa Cruz RN', 'Santa Cruz RS', 'Santa Rita', 'Santo Andre', 'Santo Andre SP', 'Santos', 'Santos AP', 'Sao Bento', 'Sao Bernardo', 'Sao Caetano', 'Sao Francisco AC', 'Sao Francisco PA', 'Sao Jose - POA', 'Sao Jose PA', 'Sao Jose RS', 'Sao Luiz', 'Sao Paulo', 'Sao Raimundo AM', 'Sao Raimundo PA', 'Sao Raimundo RR', 'Sergipe', 'Serra', 'Sete de Setembro', 'Sinop FC', 'Sobradinho', 'Sousa EC', 'Sport Recife', 'Suzano SP', 'Tocantinopolis', 'Tocantinopolis EC', 'Toledo EC', 'Tombense', 'Tombense MG', 'Trem AP', 'Treze', 'Tubarao', 'Tuna Luso', 'Tupi', 'Tupi MG', 'URT', 'URT MG', 'Uberlandia', 'Uniao Rondonopolis', 'Uniclinic CE', 'Vasco Da Gama RJ', 'Vila Nova', 'Vilhena RO', 'Vilhenense EC', 'Villa Nova', 'Vitoria', 'Vitoria EC', 'Vitoria ES', 'Vitoria da Conquista', 'Volta Redonda', 'XV Piracicaba', 'Ypiranga', 'Ypiranga AP', 'Ypiranga RS', 'tuntum EC']\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata, re\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nUFS = {\"AC\",\"AL\",\"AP\",\"AM\",\"BA\",\"CE\",\"DF\",\"ES\",\"GO\",\"MA\",\"MT\",\"MS\",\"MG\",\"PA\",\"PB\",\"PR\",\"PE\",\"PI\",\"RJ\",\"RN\",\"RS\",\"RO\",\"RR\",\"SC\",\"SP\",\"SE\",\"TO\"}\n\ndef norm(t):\n    t = unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", t).encode(\"ascii\",\"ignore\").decode().lower()\n    t = re.sub(r\"\\(.*?\\)\", \" \", t)  # remove parentheticals\n    t = re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \" \", t).strip()\n    return t\n\ndef strip_uf(t):\n    m = re.match(r\"^(.*?)\\s*-\\s*(\" + \"|\".join(UFS) + r\")$\", t)\n    if m: return m.group(1).strip(), m.group(2)\n    return t, None\n\nwith open(\"data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    brf = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nnames = sorted({r[\"home\"] for r in brf} | {r[\"away\"] for r in brf})\nprint(len(names))\nprint(names)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788203048579,"end":1788203048584}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The fixture sets are identical (380 pairs each) — wait, \"bra==novo pairs: False\" but the diff list shows pairs only in bra like ('vasco da gama-rj', 'avai-sc')... that's because novo stores \"Vasco da Gama\" WITHOUT the \"-RJ\" suffix for home but \"Botafogo-RJ\" WITH suffix away? Look: \"novo: 27/04/2019 São Paulo Botafogo-RJ\" — home \"São Paulo\" (no suffix), away \"Botafogo-RJ\" (with suffix). Inconsistent naming within novo! So pair comparison fails due to suffix inconsistency, but after stripping state suffixes the pairs should match.\n\nSo normalization must strip the \"-UF\" suffix (keeping UF as metadata) for cross-source matching. And the state info is also available in separate columns (Mandante_UF). \n\nSo the canonical match key: (comp, season, round, home_bare_key, away_bare_key) where bare_key strips state suffix. BUT the \"atletico\" ambiguity (mg/go/pr) — after stripping suffixes, \"Atletico-MG\" vs \"Atletico-GO\" both → \"atletico\"! In a pair context, round+both teams usually disambiguates... no wait, if Atletico-MG plays Atletico-GO... they're in different seasons mostly. Hmm, but as canonical keys for teams, \"atletico\" alone is ambiguous.\n\nResolution: canonical team key = bare + \"-\" + uf when uf known AND bare is ambiguous across the registry; otherwise bare. But dedupe keys need consistency: for novo row \"São Paulo\" home (uf=SP from Mandante_UF column) vs bra \"Sao Paulo-SP\" → both get uf. If bare \"sao paulo\" is unambiguous → key \"sao paulo\". If \"atletico\" ambiguous → keys \"atletico-mg\"/\"atletico-go\"/\"atletico-pr\". novo \"Atlético-MG\" home has Mandante_UF=MG → \"atletico-mg\". Good — the UF columns in novo save us. For BR-Football: \"Atletico Mineiro\" / \"Atletico GO\" / \"Atletico PR\" — different names entirely; \"atletico mineiro\" ≠ \"atletico-mg\"... need alias \"atletico mineiro\"→\"atletico-mg\". BR-Football names: let me look at the actual team names in brf to build aliases.\n\nWait, brf 2019 sample shows \"Atletico Mineiro\", \"Fortaleza FC EC Bahia\"?? \"Fortaleza FC EC Bahia\" — away team \"EC Bahia\"! Parsing: home=\"Fortaleza FC\", away=\"EC Bahia\"? The CSV columns: tournament,home,home_goal,away_goal,away,... so home=\"Fortaleza FC\" wait no: `Copa do Brasil,Sao Paulo,1.0,1.0,Flamengo,...` home=\"Sao Paulo\", away=\"Flamengo\". For brf sample above I printed r[\"date\"], r[\"home\"], r[\"away\"] → \"2019-12-08 Fortaleza FC EC Bahia\"?? No wait, that line prints home and away separately: \"brf: 2019-12-08 Fortaleza FC EC Bahia\" would mean home=\"Fortaleza FC EC Bahia\"?? No — the print is `print(\"brf:\", r[\"date\"], r[\"home\"], r[\"away\"])` → outputs \"brf: 2019-12-08 Internacional Atletico Mineiro\" = home \"Internacional\", away \"Atletico Mineiro\". Third line: \"brf: 2019-12-08 Fortaleza FC EC Bahia\" → home=\"Fortaleza FC\", away=\"EC Bahia\". OK fine.\n\nSo BR-Football names: \"Sao Paulo\", \"Flamengo\", \"Fortaleza FC\", \"EC Bahia\", \"Atletico Mineiro\", \"Atletico GO\"?, \"Corinthians\", \"Palmeiras\"... Let me dump the unique brf team names to build the alias table. Also note brf dates differ from bra dates for same fixtures (brf says 2019-12-08 for round-38-ish matches while bra dates differ). Actually wait — brf \"2019-12-08 Internacional Atletico Mineiro\" — hmm, Internacional vs Atletico-MG did happen in Dec 2019 (last round). And bra's date for that fixture? Probably also 2019-12-08. bra∩brf by (date, norm-teams-with-suffix) was 0 because of suffix mismatch (\"atletico mineiro\" vs \"atletico-mg\"). With proper normalization+aliases, date overlap might actually work! Let me check overlap with suffix-stripped + aliased names by date.\n\nPlan for canonical matching:\n1. Strip accents, lowercase.\n2. Remove state suffix \"-XX\" (also \" - XX\"), keep as uf hint.\n3. Remove noise tokens: \"fc\", \"ec\", \"ac\", \"sc\", \"aa\", \"spfc\"? careful — \"EC Bahia\" → \"bahia\" good; \"Fortaleza FC\" → \"fortaleza\"; \"Coritiba FC\"? → \"coritiba\". \"SC Coritiba\" → \"coritiba\". \"AA Ponte Preta\" → \"ponte pretta\"... \"ponte pretta\"! Note \"Ponte Preta\" (correct) vs \"Ponte Preta\"?? The file had \"Ponte Preta-SP\" in bra and novo may have \"Ponte Preta\" or \"Ponte Pretta\"? The Kaggle dataset famously has the typo \"Ponte Pretta\" in the 2003-2019 dataset. Need alias \"ponte pretta\"→\"ponte preta\".\n4. Alias table for full names: \"atletico mineiro\"→\"atletico-mg\" (with uf mg), \"atletico goianiense\"? brf uses \"Atletico GO\" → bare \"atletico\" + uf GO → \"atletico-go\". \"atletico paranaense\" → \"atletico-pr\". \"sport club do recife\"/\"sport recife\" → \"sport\". \"americA fc (minas gerais)\"... brf uses \"America FC\"? and \"America Mineiro\"? Let me dump names.\n\nFor dedupe keys I'll use (comp_key, season, round, home_key, away_key) when round is present, else (comp_key, season, home_key, away_key, date). For brf (no round): dedupe would fail to align with bra rounds... but if dates align after normalization, use date-based key for everything as PRIMARY, and round-based as fallback? Let me first measure date-based overlap after proper name canonicalization. If bra∩brf by (date, home_key, away_key) is ~380 for 2019, date-based dedupe works for those.\n\nAlso cup competitions: Brazilian_Cup_Matches vs brf \"Copa do Brasil\" (1123 rows). Round values 1-8 (numeric). Same issue.\n\nLet me now dump brf unique names and compute overlaps with canonical keys. I'll prototype the normalization function in a scratch script, then finalize.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059351e32001GoZXziGipbiuUA","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","messageID":"msg_059349da7001mccW7d0WkVcrwI"}}
