{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788203147909,"sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_7f88649265fb43f086790748","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata, re\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\nUFS = {\"AC\",\"AL\",\"AP\",\"AM\",\"BA\",\"CE\",\"DF\",\"ES\",\"GO\",\"MA\",\"MT\",\"MS\",\"MG\",\"PA\",\"PB\",\"PR\",\"PE\",\"PI\",\"RJ\",\"RN\",\"RS\",\"RO\",\"RR\",\"SC\",\"SP\",\"SE\",\"TO\"}\nNOISE = {\"fc\",\"ec\",\"ac\",\"sc\",\"clube\",\"club\",\"do\",\"da\",\"de\",\"dos\",\"das\",\"e\",\"esporte\"}\n\ndef base_norm(t):\n    t = unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", t).encode(\"ascii\",\"ignore\").decode().lower()\n    t = re.sub(r\"\\(.*?\\)\", \" \", t)\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \" \", t).strip()\n\ndef parse(t):\n    toks = base_norm(t).split()\n    uf = None\n    if len(toks) > 1 and toks[-1].upper() in UFS:\n        uf = toks[-1].upper(); toks = toks[:-1]\n    toks = [x for x in toks if x not in NOISE]\n    return \" \".join(toks), uf\n\ndef canon(name, uf=None):\n    bare, u = parse(name)\n    u = u or uf\n    if bare in (\"atletico mineiro\",): return \"atletico-mg\"\n    if bare in (\"atletico paranaense\",\"athletico paranaense\"): return \"atletico-pr\"\n    if bare == \"atletico goianiense\": return \"atletico-go\"\n    if bare in (\"sport recife\",\"sport club recife\"): return \"sport\"\n    if bare == \"cs alagoano\": return \"csa\"\n    if bare == \"america mineiro\": return \"america-mg\"\n    if u: return f\"{bare}-{u.lower()}\"\n    return bare\n\ndef load(path, **kw):\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbra = load(\"data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv\")\nnovo = load(\"data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\")\nbrf = [r for r in load(\"data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv\")]\n\n# overlap bra vs novo by (season, round, home, away)\ndef bra_k(r): return (r[\"season\"], int(r[\"round\"]), canon(r[\"home_team\"]), canon(r[\"away_team\"]))\ndef novo_k(r): return (r[\"Ano\"], int(r[\"Rodada\"]), canon(r[\"Equipe_mandante\"], r[\"Mandante_UF\"]), canon(r[\"Equipe_visitante\"], r[\"Visitante_UF\"]))\nkb = {bra_k(r) for r in bra}; kn = {novo_k(r) for r in novo}\nprint(\"bra keys:\", len(kb), \"novo keys:\", len(kn), \"overlap:\", len(kb & kn))\nby_season = Counter(s for s,_,_,_ in (kb & kn))\nprint(\"overlap by season:\", dict(sorted(by_season.items())))\n\n# overlap brf Serie A vs bra by (season, date, home, away)\ndef brf_k(r): return (r[\"date\"][:4], r[\"date\"], canon(r[\"home\"]), canon(r[\"away\"]))\nkbf = {(s,d,h,a) for s,d,h,a in (brf_k(r) for r in brf if r[\"tournament\"]==\"Serie A\")}\nkbra_d = {(r[\"datetime\"][:4], r[\"datetime\"][:10], canon(r[\"home_team\"]), canon(r[\"away_team\"])) for r in bra}\nprint(\"brf SerieA keys:\", len(kbf), \"bra date keys:\", len(kbra_d), \"date overlap:\", len(kbf & kbra_d))\n\n# same pair ignoring date within season: does brf 2019 pair-set equal bra 2019?\nb19 = {(canon(r[\"home_team\"]), canon(r[\"away_team\"])) for r in bra if r[\"season\"]==\"2019\"}\nf19 = {(canon(r[\"home\"]), canon(r[\"away\"])) for r in brf if r[\"tournament\"]==\"Serie A\" and r[\"date\"].startswith(\"2019\")}\nprint(\"2019 pair sets equal:\", b19 == f19, len(b19), len(f19))\nEOF"},"output":"bra keys: 4180 novo keys: 6886 overlap: 2346\noverlap by season: {'2012': 306, '2013': 256, '2014': 287, '2015': 306, '2016': 324, '2017': 256, '2018': 306, '2019': 305}\nbrf SerieA keys: 3689 bra date keys: 4180 date overlap: 96\n2019 pair sets equal: False 380 380\n","metadata":{"output":"bra keys: 4180 novo keys: 6886 overlap: 2346\noverlap by season: {'2012': 306, '2013': 256, '2014': 287, '2015': 306, '2016': 324, '2017': 256, '2018': 306, '2019': 305}\nbrf SerieA keys: 3689 bra date keys: 4180 date overlap: 96\n2019 pair sets equal: False 380 380\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv, unicodedata, re\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\nUFS = {\"AC\",\"AL\",\"AP\",\"AM\",\"BA\",\"CE\",\"DF\",\"ES\",\"GO\",\"MA\",\"MT\",\"MS\",\"MG\",\"PA\",\"PB\",\"PR\",\"PE\",\"PI\",\"RJ\",\"RN\",\"RS\",\"RO\",\"RR\",\"SC\",\"SP\",\"SE\",\"TO\"}\nNOISE = {\"fc\",\"ec\",\"ac\",\"sc\",\"clube\",\"club\",\"do\",\"da\",\"de\",\"dos\",\"das\",\"e\",\"esporte\"}\n\ndef base_norm(t):\n    t = unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", t).encode(\"ascii\",\"ignore\").decode().lower()\n    t = re.sub(r\"\\(.*?\\)\", \" \", t)\n    return re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \" \", t).strip()\n\ndef parse(t):\n    toks = base_norm(t).split()\n    uf = None\n    if len(toks) > 1 and toks[-1].upper() in UFS:\n        uf = toks[-1].upper(); toks = toks[:-1]\n    toks = [x for x in toks if x not in NOISE]\n    return \" \".join(toks), uf\n\ndef canon(name, uf=None):\n    bare, u = parse(name)\n    u = u or uf\n    if bare in (\"atletico mineiro\",): return \"atletico-mg\"\n    if bare in (\"atletico paranaense\",\"athletico paranaense\"): return \"atletico-pr\"\n    if bare == \"atletico goianiense\": return \"atletico-go\"\n    if bare in (\"sport recife\",\"sport club recife\"): return \"sport\"\n    if bare == \"cs alagoano\": return \"csa\"\n    if bare == \"america mineiro\": return \"america-mg\"\n    if u: return f\"{bare}-{u.lower()}\"\n    return bare\n\ndef load(path, **kw):\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(f))\n\nbra = load(\"data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv\")\nnovo = load(\"data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\")\nbrf = [r for r in load(\"data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv\")]\n\n# overlap bra vs novo by (season, round, home, away)\ndef bra_k(r): return (r[\"season\"], int(r[\"round\"]), canon(r[\"home_team\"]), canon(r[\"away_team\"]))\ndef novo_k(r): return (r[\"Ano\"], int(r[\"Rodada\"]), canon(r[\"Equipe_mandante\"], r[\"Mandante_UF\"]), canon(r[\"Equipe_visitante\"], r[\"Visitante_UF\"]))\nkb = {bra_k(r) for r in bra}; kn = {novo_k(r) for r in novo}\nprint(\"bra keys:\", len(kb), \"novo keys:\", len(kn), \"overlap:\", len(kb & kn))\nby_season = Counter(s for s,_,_,_ in (kb & kn))\nprint(\"overlap by season:\", dict(sorted(by_season.items())))\n\n# overlap brf Serie A vs bra by (season, date, home, away)\ndef brf_k(r): return (r[\"date\"][:4], r[\"date\"], canon(r[\"home\"]), canon(r[\"away\"]))\nkbf = {(s,d,h,a) for s,d,h,a in (brf_k(r) for r in brf if r[\"tournament\"]==\"Serie A\")}\nkbra_d = {(r[\"datetime\"][:4], r[\"datetime\"][:10], canon(r[\"home_team\"]), canon(r[\"away_team\"])) for r in bra}\nprint(\"brf SerieA keys:\", len(kbf), \"bra date keys:\", len(kbra_d), \"date overlap:\", len(kbf & kbra_d))\n\n# same pair ignoring date within season: does brf 2019 pair-set equal bra 2019?\nb19 = {(canon(r[\"home_team\"]), canon(r[\"away_team\"])) for r in bra if r[\"season\"]==\"2019\"}\nf19 = {(canon(r[\"home\"]), canon(r[\"away\"])) for r in brf if r[\"tournament\"]==\"Serie A\" and r[\"date\"].startswith(\"2019\")}\nprint(\"2019 pair sets equal:\", b19 == f19, len(b19), len(f19))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788203147900,"end":1788203147908}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The registry shows the ambiguity problem clearly: bare names like \"flamengo\" appear with UF RJ (major), PI (Flamengo-PI small club), None. So canonical keys must be bare-uf when ambiguous. Major clubs:\n- \"flamengo\" ambiguous {None, RJ, PI} — Flamengo-PI is a tiny Piauí club from the cup file. If I make key \"flamengo-rj\", then query \"Flamengo\" → resolves to... \"flamengo\" bare → candidates {flamengo-rj, flamengo-pi, flamengo(None)}. Hmm.\n\nBetter disambiguation heuristic: use FREQUENCY. Flamengo-RJ plays thousands of matches; Flamengo-PI plays 2 cup matches. When a bare query is ambiguous, prefer the team with most matches, but surface alternatives in the response. That gives good demo behavior: \"Flamengo\" → Flamengo (RJ).\n\nCanonical key design:\n- key = bare-uf if bare ambiguous (multiple UFs including None), else bare.\n- BUT for well-known clubs, strip to a nice canonical: I'll keep \"flamengo-rj\" as key for the big one? Then head-to-head \"Flamengo vs Fluminense\" needs \"fluminense\" (unambiguous → key \"fluminense\") vs \"flamengo\" candidates. Frequency-based auto-resolve: match_count(flamengo-rj) >> match_count(flamengo-pi) → auto-pick flamengo-rj, report \"assumed Flamengo-RJ; also found Flamengo-PI\".\n\nFor display: use the most frequent display name variant (e.g. \"Flamengo\" not \"Flamengo-RJ\"? or with state?). Display \"Flamengo (RJ)\" maybe. Keep it simple: display = most common raw name from the major sources, cleaned. I'll pick most frequent display variant overall.\n\nNow the resolution flow for a query name q:\n1. canonicalize q → (bare, uf) via parse_tokens + alias table.\n2. If alias maps to explicit key (e.g. \"atletico mineiro\" → \"atletico-mg\"), use it.\n3. If uf given and bare ambiguous → key = bare-uf; if that key exists in registry → resolved.\n4. If uf given and bare unambiguous → check contradiction: registry uf set for bare; if uf matches → key = bare; else key = bare-uf (distinct club).\n5. If no uf: if bare unambiguous → key = bare. If ambiguous → frequency-pick best, return alternatives.\n\nAlso handle 'None' uf in ambiguity: e.g. \"botafogo\" {None, PB, RJ} — Botafogo-RJ major; None entries from cup file (\"Botafogo\" without suffix in Copa do Brasil = Botafogo-RJ presumably). Hmm — cup file's bare \"Botafogo\" is probably the RJ club. The None entries pollute ambiguity. Solution: treat None-uf entries as their own key \"botafogo\" AND merge None into the most frequent uf team? For dedupe correctness (cup \"Botafogo\" vs bra \"Botafogo-RJ\" — same club, same competition? Copa do Brasil vs Brasileirão are different comps so no dedupe interaction... but standings: cup file doesn't affect league standings. Libertadores bare \"Flamengo\" vs bra \"Flamengo-RJ\" — different comps, no dedupe conflict. Team stats aggregation ACROSS competitions though! \"What is Flamengo's record?\" should merge Flamengo-RJ (brasileirao) + Flamengo (libertadores) + Flamengo (cup) + Flamengo RJ (brf). So None-uf entries must MERGE with the major club when the bare name is otherwise unambiguous-ish.\n\nRefined approach: at load time, build the registry with match counts per (bare, uf) including uf=None. Then:\n- If bare has exactly ONE uf (plus None entries) → None entries merge into that uf team; key = bare.\n- If bare has multiple UFs → each uf'd variant is its own team key bare-uf; None entries merge into the most frequent uf variant (major club).\n\nThis is a frequency-based merge — deterministic, testable, and matches \"Botafogo\"→Botafogo-RJ, \"Santos\"→Santos-SP, \"Internacional\"→Internacional-RS, \"Vitoria\"→Vitoria-BA... but WAIT: \"Vitoria\" bare with UFs {BA, ES}: cup's bare \"Vitória\" likely = Bahia's EC Vitória (most matches) ✓. \"Santos\" {None, AP, SP} → Santos-SP ✓ (Santos-AP tiny Amapá club). \"Bahia\" {BA, BH}: \"BH\"?? Bahia de Feira? \"Bahia-BH\"?? weird — BH isn't a UF... my UF set includes... no, BH is not in UFS. Where does uf=BH come from? \"Bahia de Feira - BA\"? that gives bare \"bahia de feira\" uf BA. \"bahia\" uf BH — maybe from \"EC Bahia BH\"? Hmm, in Libertadores? \"Bahia\" from cup? Let me not chase; frequency merge handles it: Bahia-BA dominant → bare \"bahia\" → key... bare has ufs {BA, BH} → ambiguous → keys \"bahia-ba\", \"bahia-bh\"; None merges into most frequent → bahia-ba. And brf \"EC Bahia\" (uf None) → merges into bahia-ba ✓.\n\nHmm wait, but this breaks display simplicity: Flamengo key = \"flamengo-rj\" (because bare ambiguous with PI). Fine — resolution auto-picks by frequency. Display name = \"Flamengo\".\n\nBUT for cross-source dedupe of matches: cup match \"Flamengo\" vs \"Athletico\" (the NA Libertadores final row) — those map to flamengo-rj / atletico-pr ✓.\n\nNow: dedupe keys. With canonical team keys, test overlap: (comp, season, round, home, away) between bra and novo 2019; and (comp, season, date, home, away) between bra and brf. Let me test.\n\nAlso — novo file: 2003-2005 were playoff formats with weird Rodada values? Rodada might be \"1\"..\"46\" or quarterfinal labels. Whatever, dedupe only matters where sources overlap (2012-2019). Let me test now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05936a205001IAN86pmL5D51XH","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","messageID":"msg_05936049c001gDtKs88k17RuVS"}}
