d 6 with 2 matches; 2016-2020 round 7 with 2 matches; 2021 round 4 with 16 matches?? — 2021 is incomplete in the dataset!). So the cup \"round\" numbers are inconsistent across seasons — the \"final\" is the MAX round of that season, not a fixed number. \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\" → matches where round == max(round) per season AND that max round has ≤2 matches (to exclude truncated 2021). I'll implement `stage=\"final\"` for Copa do Brasil as: round == max round within season and count ≤ 2. Good heuristic, testable (2013-2020 finals ≈ 16 matches, 2012's round 6 = 2 matches final).\n\nHmm wait 2012: rounds 1-6, round 6 has 2 matches → final (two-legged, correct: 2012 final Palmeiras vs Coritiba two legs ✓). 2021: rounds 1-4 with round 4 = 16 matches (round of 32?) — dataset truncated mid-season; round 4 ≠ final → excluded by the ≤2 rule ✓.\n\npytest-bdd didn't show install output properly — let me check it installed.\n\nNow let me write all the code. Plan of files:\n\n**brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py**:\n- `UFS`, `STATE_NAMES` (for parentheticals), `NOISE_TOKENS`\n- `ALIASES` dict (curated)\n- `strip_accents`, `base_norm`, `parse_team_name(name) -> (bare, uf)`\n- `parse_date(s) -> date | None` handling \"YYYY-MM-DD[ HH:MM:SS]\", \"DD/MM/YYYY\", \"NA\"/\"-\"\n- `parse_int(s) -> int | None` handling \"2\", \"-\", \"\", \"NA\", floats \"1.0\"\n- `TeamRegistry` class: built from (display, uf, count) observations; method `canonical(display, uf=None) -> key`; `display(key)`; `resolve(query) -> ResolveResult(key, display, alternatives)`.\n\nRegistry building: two passes.\n- Pass 1: scan all match files, for each (display, uf_hint) → parse → (bare, uf) → accumulate counts per (bare, uf) and display-variant counts per key.\n- Pass 2: decide keys:\n  - For each bare: ufs_with_counts = {uf: count} (uf may be None).\n  - Let non_none = {uf:count for uf,count in ufs if uf}\n  - If len(non_none) <= 1: key = bare; all matches (any uf incl None) → key.\n  - Else (multiple ufs): for each uf → key = f\"{bare}-{uf}\"; None-uf matches → merge into most frequent uf's key.\n  \n  Wait, subtle: bra \"Flamengo-RJ\" gives bare \"flamengo\" uf RJ. cup \"Flamengo\" gives bare \"flamengo\" uf None. Libertadores \"Barcelona-EQU\" → \"EQU\" not UF → bare \"barcelona equa\"?? NO — \"Barcelona-EQU\" parse: tokens [barcelona, equ]; \"equ\" not in UFS → uf stays None, bare = \"barcelona equa\"?? base_norm(\"Barcelona-EQU\") = \"barcelona equ\" — tokens [barcelona, equ] — last token \"equ\" not in UFS → bare \"barcelona equ\". Hmm that's wrong-ish but consistent within Libertadores (all foreign teams with -EQU suffix → \"barcelona equ\"?? wait \"Barcelona-EQU\" → the suffix -EQU means Ecuador). For matching purposes, all Libertadores foreign teams are consistently named within that file, so search within Libertadores works. Query \"Barcelona\" → bare \"barcelona\" → hmm, \"barcelona equ\" ≠ \"barcelona\" → no match. Edge case; acceptable. Actually — better: ALSO strip 2-4 letter all-caps suffixes? \"Nacional (URU)\" → parenthetical removed → \"nacional\". \"Barcelona-EQU\" vs \"Barcelona\" — let me add suffix strip for known country codes {URU, ARG, EQU, COL, CHI, PAR, BOL, PER, VEN, MEX}? \"Nacional (URU)\" → bare \"nacional\" — then \"nacional\" registry: bare with uf None only → key \"nacional\". OK I'll strip trailing country codes too (after UFS check). Cheap win for Libertadores queries.\n\n- Canonicalization must be STABLE across the two passes — I'll compute the key-mapping (bare+uf→key) once at load, then canonicalize every match row with it. The registry also stores display names: display[key] = most frequent display variant (prettiest). For \"flamengo-rj\" → most frequent display is... bra file has \"Flamengo-RJ\" 200+ times, cup \"Flamengo\", lib \"Flamengo\"... display = \"Flamengo-RJ\"? Hmm, display as \"Flamengo\" is nicer for LLM output. Preference: display WITHOUT suffix if available — choose the most frequent display variant that has no state suffix? For \"flamengo-rj\": \"Flamengo\" appears in cup+lib many times → display \"Flamengo\" ✓. For \"atletico-mg\": displays \"Atletico-MG\", \"Atlético-MG\", \"Atlético Mineiro\"? (brf) → prefer... any. Fine: prefer most-frequent display without UF suffix; fallback most frequent with.\n\n- `resolve(query)`: parse query → if alias hits, return that key. If uf present → key candidate f\"{bare}-{uf}\" if exists, elif bare exists and bare's uf set == {uf} → bare, elif f\"{bare}-{uf}\" not in registry but bare exists with different uf → NOT FOUND (contradiction) — hmm or bare? e.g. query \"Vitoria-ES\" vs registry vitoria-ba... report not found with suggestion. If no uf: bare in registry → if bare is a KEY (unambiguous) → it. Else ambiguous → frequency-rank the bare-uf keys, pick top, alternatives = rest. Also try containment: bare not exact → keys whose bare-part contains query bare or vice versa? For fuzzy queries (\"Fla\"?) skip — exact bare matching + aliases covers the spec. Maybe substring fallback: query \"palmeiras\" exact ✓. Query \"corinthians paulista\"? \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" from spec's naming example! tokens: [sport, club, corinthians, paulista] → remove club → \"sport corinthians paulista\" ≠ \"corinthians\". Hmm! The spec explicitly mentions full names like \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" as a variation to handle. My NOISE removal: \"sport\" NOT removed (Sport club!), \"paulista\" not removed. Fallback matching: if exact bare miss, try matching by checking whether any registry key's bare contains ALL query tokens (set containment): query tokens {sport, corinthians, paulista} ⊆ key bare tokens {corinthians}? No. Other direction: key tokens ⊆ query tokens: {corinthians} ⊆ {sport, corinthians, paulista} ✓ → match corinthians! Implement: after exact miss, find keys whose token set is a subset of the query token set (ignoring noise tokens already removed). If exactly one → match; if several → pick by frequency, report alternatives