ves club/do → \"sport recife\" → alias → \"sport\" ✓. FIFA \"Ceará Sporting Club\" → tokens [ceara, sporting, club] → remove club → \"ceara sporting\" → hmm alias \"ceara sporting\"→\"ceara\" — add. FIFA \"Bahia\"/\"Botafogo\"/\"Santos\"/\"Flamengo\" → bare freq merge ✓. FIFA \"Athletico Paranaense\"? maybe — alias covers. FIFA \"Chapecoense\" ✓. FIFA \"Sport Club do Recife\" ✓ via alias. FIFA \"Goiás\" ✓. FIFA \"Cuiabá\"? \"Cuiaba\" bare — registry \"cuiaba\" ufs {MT} → \"cuiaba\" ✓ (bra \"Cuiaba-MT\"). Hmm wait bra name \"Cuiaba-MT\" → bare \"cuiaba\" uf MT; brf \"Cuiaba\"/\"Cuiaba MT\" ✓ all merge.\n\nLet me also double-check \"vasco\": lib has \"Vasco\" bare (no suffix, no uf). registry \"vasco da gama\" {RJ} unambiguous → key \"vasco da gama\"; lib \"Vasco\" → bare \"vasco\" ≠ \"vasco da gama\"!! distinct key \"vasco\". Alias needed: \"vasco\"→\"vasco da gama\" ✓ (already planned).\n\nAlso cup file: does it have bare \"Vasco\"? All cup names seem suffixed. And what about \"Sao Paulo\" in novo: \"São Paulo\" bare + Mandante_UF=SP → uf SP ✓ merges with bra \"Sao Paulo-SP\" → bare \"sao paulo\" unambiguous {SP} → key \"sao paulo\" ✓.\n\nOne more: novo \"Paraná\" + UF PR ✓. novo \"Athletico-PR\" → bare \"athletico\" uf PR → alias \"athletico-pr\"→\"atletico-pr\" ✓. And bra \"Atletico-PR\" → bare \"atletico\" uf PR → key \"atletico-pr\" ✓ same. Registry bare \"atletico\" ufs {ES,MG,GO,BA,AC,PR} → multiple → keys atletico-es/atletico-mg/atletigo-go/atletico-ba/atletico-ac/atletico-pr; None-uf (lib \"Athletico\"? that's bare \"athletico\" separate!) — lib \"Athletico\" → alias direct → atletico-pr ✓. lib \"Atlético-MG\" ✓ suffixed. Good.\n\nWhat bare \"atletico\" uf=None entries exist? cup file? cup names all suffixed... \"Atlético - MG\"? suffix ✓. OK.\n\nAlright — enough. Time to WRITE THE CODE. Let me be decisive and write the full implementation now. Files:\n\n1. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/__init__.py`\n2. `brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py` — ~200 lines\n3. `brazilian