ro\": \"america-mg\",\n  \"america fc minas gerais\": \"america-mg\",  # unreachable (parenthetical stripped) but harmless\n  \"vasco\": \"vasco da gama\",\n  \"ceara sporting\": \"ceara\",\n  \"bragantino-sp\": \"red bull bragantino\",\n  \"libertad\": \"libertad-PAR\",  # hmm — display? keep simple \"libertad-par\"? I'll normalize country suffixes to lowercase too. \"libertad-par\".\n}\n```\nHmm wait: alias values must be keys that will exist in the registry. \"red bull bragantino\" — bra \"Red Bull Bragantino-SP\" → bare \"red bull bragantino\" uf SP → unambiguous → key \"red bull bragantino\" ✓. But \"bragantino-sp\" alias input: parse(\"Bragantino-SP\")→(bragantino, SP) → alias key \"bragantino-sp\" → target \"red bull bragantino\" ✓.\n\nRegistry build:\n```python\nclass TeamRegistry:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._counts = {}      # (bare, uf) -> match count\n        self._displays = {}    # key -> {display: count}\n        self._key_map = {}     # (bare, uf, country) -> key   (country only from explicit suffix)\n        self._keys = set()\n```\nTwo-phase:\n- observe(display, uf=None): parse → bare, uf, country; count[(bare, uf)] += 1; display count.\n- finalize(): for each bare: ufs = {uf for (b,uf) in counts if b==bare}; non_none = ufs - {None};\n  - if len(non_none) <= 1: single team: key = bare; map ALL (bare, uf) → key (uf None or the single uf).\n  - else: for uf in non_none: key = f\"{bare}-{uf}\"; map (bare, uf) → key; map (bare, None) → most frequent uf key.\n  - country handling: (bare, None, country) → key f\"{bare}-{country.lower()}\"; (bare, uf, country)? unlikely; if country present and uf None and bare has single non-none uf... hmm country teams (foreign) — bare like \"nacional\" only from lib with country codes → key \"nacional-uru\"/\"nacional-par\" distinct. But if a bare has BOTH uf entries and country entries?? e.g. \"libertad\"? lib only. \"guarani\"? lib only (Guaraní PAR). OK: if country present → key f\"{bare}-{country.lower()}