on_dict(team_res)\n    opponent_key = None\n    if opponent:\n        opp_res = self.registry.resolve(opponent)\n        if not opp_res.found: return error\n        opponent_key = opp_res.key\n        payload[\"opponent\"] = self._resolution_dict(opp_res)\n\n    comp_key = None\n    if competition:\n        comp_key = self._resolve_competition_key(competition)\n        if comp_key is None: return error\n        payload[\"competition\"] = COMPETITIONS[comp_key]\n\n    if source:\n        pool = self.matches\n        if comp_key: pool = [m for m in pool if m.competition_key == comp_key]\n        if season is not None: pool = [m for m in pool if m.season == season]\n        pool = [m for m in pool if m.source == source]\n    else:\n        pool = self._pool(competition, season)   # resolved, comp+season aware\n    if team_key:\n        pool = [m for m in pool if m.involves(team_key)]\n    if opponent_key:\n        pool = [m for m in pool if m.involves_pair(team_key or opponent_key, opponent_key)]\n    ...\n```\n\nWait — `_pool(competition, season)` signature: `_pool(competition, season, source)` takes competition as STRING and resolves internally. In search I already resolved comp_key; passing competition string again re-resolves — fine but let me pass the string.\n\nAlso in `_pool` when season is not None and comp is None: `[m for m in self._resolved_matches if m.season == season]` ✓.\n\nAlso `_build_match` has awkward `home=` expression with `and` — clean up.\n\nAlso head_to_head uses `self._by_team` (resolved) ✓ good — h2h shouldn't have duplicates.\n\nFix _match_finals: uses `self._pool(comp_key, season_value)` — comp_key string \"copa-do-brasil\" → _resolve_competition_key(\"copa-do-brasil\") → norm_text match ✓ works.\n\nBut note `_match_finals(comp_key, None)` inside _stage_filter iterates ALL seasons of the comp — but the matches passed in may be already season-filtered. The finals set computed for all seasons still applies per-match id matching ✓ correct.\n\nAlso in `_stage_filter` for stage \"final\" with comp \"copa-do-brasil\": matches from multiple comps? The loop `for comp_key in {m.competition_key for m in matches}` handles each comp's matches with its logic; for league comps, no stage==\"final\" labels exist so nothing matches — fine.\n\nLet me rewrite those two functions cleanly.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059416177001m1sOE2TxHv6F1m","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","messageID":"msg_0594122320012TgQlQF1A6OVvU"}}
