ns home record 19 matches 11W 5D 3L — that does NOT match this data (which gives 15 with results, 10W 4D 1L). The spec's examples are illustrative formats, not data assertions. I'll assert data-truth values in tests.\n\nFIFA data has NO Flamengo/Corinthians/Palmeiras/São Paulo/Vasco clubs — so \"players at Flamengo\" queries return empty truthfully. The spec example \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\" would return \"no players found\". Hmm wait — but that makes some spec sample questions unanswerable. Let me double-check the FIFA data — maybe club names for those clubs are like \"CR Flamengo\"? The search showed no club containing \"fla\" at all! So genuinely absent. But WAIT — Santos, Grêmio, Fluminense, Botafogo ARE present. This looks like FIFA 18, which licensed only SOME Brazilian clubs? Actually FIFA 18/19 famously did NOT include Corinthians, Flamengo, Palmeiras, São Paulo, Vasco (they're in PES instead!). Exactly — EA didn't have licenses for those 5 clubs; PES had them. So the data is authentically FIFA 18. ✓ my implementation correctly returns 0.\n\nFor the test \"who plays for Flamengo\" — I'll test with clubs that exist (Santos, Grêmio, Fluminense). And a test that Flamengo query returns empty gracefully (total 0, no error).\n\nplayers_by_club shows 16 clubs — matches the 16 licensed Brazilian clubs with Brazilian squads. Let me verify it's exactly the set of FIFA Brazilian clubs: América FC (MG), Chapecoense, Atlético Paranaense, Bahia, Botafogo, Paraná, Santos, Grêmio, Sport Club do Recife, Ceará Sporting Club, Atlético Mineiro, Cruzeiro, Vitória, Fluminense, Internacional, + maybe one more = 16 ✓ plausible.\n\nNow fix the derby key: \"fluminense\" → \"fluminense-rj\". Also \"corinthians\" ✓, \"sao paulo\" ✓ — wait is \"sao paulo\" single-uf? bra \"Sao Paulo-SP\" only + brf \"Sao Paulo\" + novo \"São Paulo\"+UF SP → single {SP} → key \"sao paulo\" ✓ (resolve earlier confirmed). \"palmeiras\" ✓. \"vasco da gama\" ✓ — vasco in lib is bare \"Vasco\" → alias → \"vasco da gama\" ✓. \"botafogo-rj\" ✓.\n\nAlso check display for \"fluminense-rj\" → \"Fluminense\" ✓ (shown in resolve output).\n\nFix DERBIES entry. Then also fix the earlier smoke-test issue: `svc.registry._brazilian_team_keys` was my script bug (it's on service not registry) — fine.\n\nAlso \"America MG\" display for america-mg — display picked brf name. Let me check display counts... minor cosmetic. Actually let me look: registry.display(\"america-mg\") → ? The earlier players_by_club output showed \"America MG\". Displays for key america-mg: \"America-MG\" (bra), \"América-MG\"/\"América\" (novo), \"America MG\" (brf), \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" (fifa), \"América - MG\" (cup)... count: bra has América-MG Serie A appearances 2012-2022: 2012? América-MG was in Serie A 2016,2017? no wait. Hmm — bra covers only Serie A. América-MG Serie A seasons: 2016, 2017? no... Let me count: América-MG in Serie A 2012-2022: 2012? No (Serie B). 2016 yes, 2017 yes, 2018? no. 2019? no. 2021 yes, 2022 yes. So ~4 seasons × 38 = 152 matches × 2? no — each match mentions América-MG once (home or away) → ~152 mentions. novo (2003-2019): América-MG Serie A seasons 2003? no. 2004? no... 2005 yes, 2006? no, 2007? no, 2008 no, 2009 no, 2010 no, 2011 no, 2012 no, 2013 no, 2014 no, 2015 no, 2016 yes, 2017 yes... ~2-3 seasons → ~100. brf: América MG in Serie A 2016,2017,2021,2022 + Serie B 2015,2018,2019,2020,2023? + Serie C? + Copa do Brasil → many! Serie B has 380 matches/season — América-MG Serie B ~2015,2018,2019,2020,2023 → 5×38=190 + Serie A 152 + cup ~15 → ~350 mentions. So \"America MG\" (brf, ~350) beats \"America-MG\" (bra, ~152). Display = \"America MG\". Cosmetic — acceptable (it IS a legit display from the data). Could prefer bra-file displays but not worth complexity.\n\nNext: fix DERBIES, then check derby detection works for Fla-Flu. Then write tests. Also double-check `search_players` club filter logic bug:\n\n```python\nif club_norm:\n    if (club_key and player.club_key == club_key):\n        pass\n    elif club_norm not in norm_text(player.club):\n        continue\n```\nThe `pass` branch: when club_key matches player's club_key → included ✓. When club_key is truthy but doesn't match → falls to elif: club_norm in player.club display? e.g. club=\"Fluminense\" → club_key=\"fluminense-rj\"; player at Fluminense-PI (fifa? none) — fine. But logic reads awkwardly; acceptable.\n\nOne more check — search_players(name=\"Gabriel Barbosa\") → \"M. Barbosa\"? name_norm \"gabriel barbosa\" ⊄ \"m barbosa\" → 0 results. Spec Q \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" → empty result... The data has no Gabigol (he's at Flamengo... wait Gabigol was at Inter Milan/ Santos on FIFA 18? \"Gabriel Barbosa\" — FIFA 18: at Inter? Hmm \"M. Barbosa\" at Villarreal is Mario Barbosa? Whatever). search_players(name=\"Barbosa\") finds 3 ✓. Test will use \"Neymar\" etc.\n\nNow: the FIFA \"Value\"/\"Wage\" columns — fine as raw strings.\n\nLet me fix the DERBIES and re-run derby check.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059445d90001IIxhP222ZpltFh","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","messageID":"msg_05943c7bb001lvk6qhuulDb0Ac"}}
