eries.py — BDD steps for match_queries.feature\n  test_team_queries.py — BDD steps for team_queries.feature\n  test_player_queries.py — BDD steps\n  test_competition_queries.py — BDD steps\n  test_statistics_queries.py — BDD steps\n  test_mcp_server.py — in-process MCP protocol test\n\npytest-bdd 8.1 usage:\n```python\nfrom pytest_bdd import scenarios, given, when, then, parsers\nscenarios(\"features/match_queries.feature\")\n```\nscenarios path relative to the test file. Feature files:\n\n**features/match_queries.feature**:\n```gherkin\nFeature: Match Queries\n  As a soccer fan asking questions in natural language\n  I want to search the match datasets\n  So that I can find fixtures, scores and competitions\n\n  Scenario: Find matches between two teams\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n    Then I should receive a list of matches\n    And each match should have date, scores, and competition\n\n  Scenario: Find matches for a team in a season\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I search for matches of team \"Palmeiras\" in season 2023\n    Then I should receive a list of matches\n    And every match should involve Palmeiras\n    And every match should be from season 2023\n\n  Scenario: Find all Copa do Brasil finals\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I search for finals of competition \"Copa do Brasil\"\n    Then every match should be from competition Copa do Brasil\n    And each season should contribute at most 2 finals\n\n  Scenario: Find matches by date range\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I search for matches from \"2019-11-01\" to \"2019-11-30\" in competition \"Brasileirão Série A\" season 2019\n    Then every match should fall within the date range\n    And the result should not be empty\n\n  Scenario: Find the most recent match between two teams\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Corinthians\"\n    Then the last match should be the most recent Fla x Corinthians fixture\n```\n\nHmm — keep scenarios focused and step-def reusable. Let me design steps:\n\n- Given \"the match data is loaded\" → svc fixture (session-scoped)\n- When 'I search for matches between \"{a}\" and \"{b}\"' → svc.search_matches(team=a, opponent=b)\n- When 'I search for matches of team \"{team}\" in season {season}' \n- When 'I search for finals of competition \"{comp}\"' → search_matches(competition=comp, stage=\"final\", limit=500)\n- When 'I search for matches from \"{from}\" to \"{to}\" in competition \"{comp}\" season {season}'\n- Then \"I should receive a list of matches\" → total>0, matches list\n- Then \"each match should have date, scores, and competition\"\n- Then \"every match should involve Palmeiras\" — parameterized: 'every match should involve \"{team}\"'\n- Then \"every match should be from season {season}\"\n- Then 'every match should be from competition \"{comp}\"'\n- Then \"each season should contribute at most 2 finals\"\n- Then \"every match should fall within the date range\"\n- Then \"the result should not be empty\"\n- Then \"the last match should be the most recent Fla x Corinthians fixture\" — too specific; make generic: 'the last match should be on \"{date}\"' → assert last_match date == 2023-10-08? For Fla x Cor: last is 2023-10-08 Corinthians 1-1 Flamengo. Assert result[\"matches\"][-1][\"date\"] == \"2023-10-08\". That's a solid data-grounded assertion.\n\n**features/team_queries.feature**:\n```gherkin\nFeature: Team Queries\n\n  Scenario: Get team statistics for a season\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season 2023\n    Then I should receive wins, losses, draws, and goals\n    And the totals should be consistent\n\n  Scenario: Get a team's home record in a season\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I request home statistics for \"Corinthians\" in season 2022\n    Then I should receive wins, losses, draws, and goals\n    And the home record should count 15 played matches\n\n  Scenario: Compare two teams head-to-head\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I compare \"Palmeiras\" and \"Santos\" head-to-head\n    Then I should receive their matches and an all-time record\n    And the record should account for every match with a result\n\n  Scenario: List competitions a team played in\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I list the competitions of \"Palmeiras\"\n    Then Palmeiras should appear in Brasileirão Série A, Copa do Brasil and Copa Libertadores\n\n  Scenario: Resolve team name variations\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I resolve the team name \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"\n    Then it should resolve to Corinthians\n```\n\n**features/player_queries.feature**:\n```gherkin\nFeature: Player Queries\n\n  Scenario: Search a player by name\n    Given the player data is loaded\n    When I search for players named \"Neymar\"\n    Then Neymar Jr should be found with an overall rating\n\n  Scenario: Find the top Brazilian players\n    Given the player data is loaded\n    When I request the top 3 Brazilian players\n    Then Neymar Jr should lead the list\n\n  Scenario: Find players at a Brazilian club\n    Given the player data is loaded\n    When I search for Brazilian players at club \"Santos\"\n    Then every result should play for Santos\n\n  Scenario: Show all forwards from a club\n    Given the player data is loaded\n    When I search for forwards at club \"Grêmio\"\n    Then every result should be a forward position\n\n  Scenario: Brazilian players by Brazilian club\n    Given the player data is loaded\n    When I aggregate Brazilian players by club\n    Then each listed club should be a Brazilian club with player counts\n```\n\n**features/competition_queries.feature**:\n```gherkin\nFeature: Competition Queries\n\n  Scenario: Who won the 2019 Brasileirão\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I request the standings of \"Brasileirão Série A\" season 2019\n    Then Flamengo should be champion with 90 points\n    And the table should have 20 teams\n    And Santos should be second with 74 points\n\n  Scenario: Which teams were relegated in 2019\n    ...relegated should be Avaí, Chapecoense, CSA and Cruzeiro (order bottom-up: rows[-4:] = [Cruzeiro, Chapecoense, CSA, Avaí]? my implementation: rows[-4:] in table order (17th..20th) = Cruzeiro(36), Chapecoense(32), CSA(32), Avaí(20). Assert set equality.\n\n  Scenario: Standings for cups are rejected\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I request the standings of \"Copa do Brasil\" season 2019\n    Then the response should explain that cups have no standings\n\n  Scenario: Competition info lists seasons and sources\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I request competition info\n    Then five competitions should be described\n    And the Copa Libertadores should cover 2013 to 2022\n```\n\n**features/statistics_queries.feature**:\n```gherkin\nFeature: Statistical Analysis\n\n  Scenario: Average goals per match in the Brasileirão\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I request league statistics for \"Brasileirão Série A\"\n    Then the average goals per match should be between 2 and 3\n    And the home win rate should be higher than the away win rate\n\n  Scenario: Biggest wins in the dataset\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I request the 5 biggest wins\n    Then the largest margin should be at least 8 goals\n    And wins should be ordered by decreasing margin\n\n  Scenario: Best home record\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I request the best home records in \"Brasileirão Série A\"\n    Then the records should be ranked by win rate\n\n  Scenario: Derbies\n    Given the match data is loaded\n    When I request derby matches\n    Then the Fla-Flu derby should be listed\n    And the Gre-Nal derby should be listed\n```\n\nThen test_mcp_server.py — in-memory MCP protocol test:\n```pytho