{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788204178319,"sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_2a03a9c765c74328ab3d6f1c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.service import SoccerDataService\nsvc = SoccerDataService(\"data/kaggle\")\nfor season in (2018, 2020, 2021, 2023):\n    st = svc.standings(\"Brasileirão Série A\", season)\n    if \"error\" in st:\n        print(season, \"ERROR:\", st[\"error\"]); continue\n    rows = st[\"table\"]\n    print(season, \"matches:\", st[\"matches_considered\"], \"champion:\", st[\"champion\"], \"relegated:\", st[\"relegated\"])\n    top_scorer = max(rows, key=lambda r: r[\"goals_for\"])\n    print(\"   most goals:\", top_scorer[\"display\"], top_scorer[\"goals_for\"], \"| top pts:\", rows[0][\"display\"], rows[0][\"points\"])\n    print(\"   teams:\", len(rows))\nEOF"},"output":"2018 matches: 380 champion: Palmeiras relegated: ['Sport', 'America MG', 'Vitoria', 'Parana']\n   most goals: Palmeiras 64 | top pts: Palmeiras 80\n   teams: 20\n2020 matches: 380 champion: Flamengo relegated: ['Vasco Da Gama RJ', 'Goiás', 'Coritiba', 'Botafogo-RJ']\n   most goals: Flamengo 68 | top pts: Flamengo 71\n   teams: 20\n2021 matches: 380 champion: Atlético-MG relegated: ['Grêmio', 'EC Bahia', 'Sport', 'Chapecoense']\n   most goals: Flamengo 69 | top pts: Atlético-MG 84\n   teams: 20\n2023 matches: 377 champion: Grêmio relegated: ['Vasco Da Gama RJ', 'Goiás', 'Coritiba', 'America MG']\n   most goals: Grêmio 63 | top pts: Grêmio 68\n   teams: 20\n","metadata":{"output":"2018 matches: 380 champion: Palmeiras relegated: ['Sport', 'America MG', 'Vitoria', 'Parana']\n   most goals: Palmeiras 64 | top pts: Palmeiras 80\n   teams: 20\n2020 matches: 380 champion: Flamengo relegated: ['Vasco Da Gama RJ', 'Goiás', 'Coritiba', 'Botafogo-RJ']\n   most goals: Flamengo 68 | top pts: Flamengo 71\n   teams: 20\n2021 matches: 380 champion: Atlético-MG relegated: ['Grêmio', 'EC Bahia', 'Sport', 'Chapecoense']\n   most goals: Flamengo 69 | top pts: Atlético-MG 84\n   teams: 20\n2023 matches: 377 champion: Grêmio relegated: ['Vasco Da Gama RJ', 'Goiás', 'Coritiba', 'America MG']\n   most goals: Grêmio 63 | top pts: Grêmio 68\n   teams: 20\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.service import SoccerDataService\nsvc = SoccerDataService(\"data/kaggle\")\nfor season in (2018, 2020, 2021, 2023):\n    st = svc.standings(\"Brasileirão Série A\", season)\n    if \"error\" in st:\n        print(season, \"ERROR:\", st[\"error\"]); continue\n    rows = st[\"table\"]\n    print(season, \"matches:\", st[\"matches_considered\"], \"champion:\", st[\"champion\"], \"relegated:\", st[\"relegated\"])\n    top_scorer = max(rows, key=lambda r: r[\"goals_for\"])\n    print(\"   most goals:\", top_scorer[\"display\"], top_scorer[\"goals_for\"], \"| top pts:\", rows[0][\"display\"], rows[0][\"points\"])\n    print(\"   teams:\", len(rows))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788204178301,"end":1788204178317}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The tool works — it returns JSON as TextContent (the dict is serialized into text content), not structured content. That's the mcp 2.x behavior for dict returns when `structured_output` is not forced. Fine — the tool result is JSON text, which LLM clients parse. For the test I'll parse the JSON text from `res.content[0].text`.\n\nNow write all the tests. Plan:\n\n- tests/conftest.py: session-scoped `service` fixture (loads once, ~1s), DATA_DIR resolution.\n- tests/features/*.feature (5 files)\n- tests/test_normalize.py — unit tests\n- tests/test_loaders.py — load counts\n- tests/test_match_queries.py + steps\n- tests/test_team_queries.py\n- tests/test_player_queries.py\n- tests/test_competition_queries.py\n- tests/test_statistics_queries.py\n- tests/test_mcp_server.py — protocol test (anyio + asyncio task, parse JSON text)\n- tests/test_sample_questions.py — the \"at least 20 sample questions\" criterion: a parametrized test answering 20+ spec-style questions end-to-end. This directly addresses the Data Coverage success criterion. I'll implement it as pytest.mark.parametrize with (question, checker) or just sequential asserts in one test... Better: parametrize over question ids with expected assertions. Let me build a table of 22 questions:\n\n1. \"When did Flamengo last play Corinthians?\" → search_matches(team, opponent) → last match 2023-10-08\n2. \"What was the score?\" (same result carries score \"1-1\")\n3. \"Who is Neymar?\" → search_players(name=\"Neymar\") → Neymar Jr, overall 92\n4. \"Which players play for Santos?\" (Brazilian club present in FIFA) → total ≥ 15\n5. \"Show me all derbies in 2023\" → derbies(season=2023) ≥ 3 derbies\n6. \"What competitions has Palmeiras played in?\" → 3 competitions\n7. \"Which team has the best home record?\" → best_records(venue=home) top = Grêmio\n8. \"Who are the top Brazilian players?\" → Neymar first\n9. \"Compare the 2018 and 2019 seasons\" → league_statistics for both seasons\n10. \"Show me all Flamengo vs Fluminense matches\" → h2h ≥ 40\n11. \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\" → ≥ 40\n12. \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\" → 18 finals\n13. \"What is Corinthians' home record in 2022?\" → 15 matches w/ results\n14. \"Which team scored the most goals in Serie A 2023?\" → standings(2023) max goals_for team\n15. \"Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head\" → h2h\n16. \"Who won the 2019 Brasileirão?\" → Flamengo\n17. \"Which teams were relegated in 2020?\" → standings(2020) bottom 4 — wait 2020 results complete? 2020 season in bra file: 380 matches; missing results? Corinthians 2022 had 4 missing. Check 2020 relegated real: Coritiba, Botafogo, Vasco? no wait 2020 relegated: Coritiba, Botafogo, Vasco, Goiás? Actually 2020 Série A relegated: Coritiba, Botafogo, Vasco da Gama, Goiás... hmm no — 2020 relegated four: Coritiba, Botafogo, Vasco, and... Sport? Let me not rely on memory — compute from data in the test as bottom-4 of the computed table and assert membership of specific teams only if verified. Safer: assert relegated has 4 entries and they match the last 4 rows of table. I'll check 2020 data completeness first.\n18. \"What's the average goals per match in the Brasileirão?\" → 2.57 (assert 2.0-3.0)\n19. \"Which team has the best away record?\" → best_records(venue=away)\n20. \"Show me the biggest wins in the dataset\" → margin ≥ 8\n21. \"Show the Libertadores finals\" → search stage=final → 15\n22. \"Find all Brazilian players\" → search_players(nationality=Brazil) total 827\n23. \"Who are the highest rated players at Grêmio?\" → top_players(club=\"Grêmio\")\n24. \"Show me all forwards from São Paulo FC\" → search_players(club=?, position=forward) — São Paulo FC not in FIFA data → returns empty gracefully. Use Grêmio instead? The spec question uses São Paulo FC — data truth: 0. I'll include it asserting graceful empty (documents data coverage).\n25. \"What did the 2019 Copa do Brasil final look like?\" — cup finals 2019 → 2 matches.\n\nAlso BDD features cover the two spec-given scenarios verbatim-ish. \n\nCheck 2020 relegation data first, and goals leader 2023 (brf 2023 data: 377/380 matches — completeness?). Let me verify quickly. Also 2018 stats for #9.\n\nAlso — one subtle thing about `standings(2023)`: brf 2023 Serie A with 377 matches. Table of 20 teams; \"most goals scored\" = table[0] by goals_for? I'll compute max goals row.\n\nLet me verify 2020 and 2023 standings quickly.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059465837001gCQm2SzDzM4eBa","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","messageID":"msg_05945f948001QiX709DEkdfoHC"}}
