"flamengo-rj\") returned \"Flamengo\" (lib/cup uses bare Flamengo many times). For the synthetic test, plain name loses on count. I could change the test to observe \"Flamengo\" enough times, or change preference: prefer no-suffix FIRST then count? That would make \"Fla\" (no suffix) always preferred even if rare... For real data it worked because bare was frequent. I think preferring simple names when they exist AT ALL is better for LLM display (e.g. \"Vasco da Gama\" over \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\"? hmm). Let me flip priority: (simple, count, -len)? Then for a team whose only display is \"Fluminense PI\" → stays. For \"fluminense-rj\": displays include \"Fluminense\" (lib/cup/bare) and \"Fluminense-RJ\"/\"Fluminense RJ\" → picks \"Fluminense\" ✓. For \"atletico-mg\": displays \"Atletico-MG\", \"Atlético-MG\", \"Atletico Mineiro\", \"Atlético Mineiro\"? \"Atletico Mineiro\" has no \"-\" → preferred → display \"Atlético Mineiro\"?? Hmm, that changes real displays. Is that bad? \"Atlético Mineiro\" is a fine display. But earlier smoke tests asserted display == \"Flamengo\", \"Corinthians\", \"Grêmio\", \"Palmeiras\" — those are unaffected. But sample-questions tests use display in relegated_2020 expecting \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\"... that test expects the brf name! If I flip preference, display(\"vasco da gama\") becomes \"Vasco\" or \"Vasco da Gama\" (bra \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\", lib \"Vasco\", brf \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\", novo \"Vasco da Gama\"+UF...). With simple-first: candidates without \"-\": \"Vasco\" (lib, ~10), \"Vasco da Gama\" (novo, ~300) → count → \"Vasco da Gama\". So relegated would be \"Vasco da Gama\", \"Goiás\", \"Coritiba\", \"Botafogo\" (botafogo-rj displays: \"Botafogo\" (lib/cup) vs \"Botafogo-RJ\" → \"Botafogo\" preferred). Hmm those become nicer actually! And Grêmio/Coritiba/Goiás unaffected. I'd need to update the test expectation to {\"Vasco da Gama\", \"Goiás\", \"Coritiba\", \"Botafogo\"}.\n\nLet me flip to (simple, count, -len) and update the two affected