{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788204530716,"sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_fed6e89d193b4bfd920227cc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nfor path, cols in [\n    (\"data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv\", [\"home_team\",\"away_team\"]),\n    (\"data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\", [\"home_team\",\"away_team\"]),\n    (\"data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv\", [\"home_team\",\"away_team\"]),\n    (\"data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv\", [\"home\",\"away\"]),\n    (\"data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\", [\"Equipe_mandante\",\"Equipe_visitante\"]),\n]:\n    c = Counter()\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for col in cols:\n                v = row[col].strip()\n                if \"vasco\" in v.lower():\n                    c[v] += 1\n    print(path.split(\"/\")[-1], dict(c))\nEOF"},"output":"Brasileirao_Matches.csv {'Vasco da Gama-RJ': 266}\nBrazilian_Cup_Matches.csv {'Vasco da Gama - RJ': 54}\nLibertadores_Matches.csv {'Vasco': 6}\nBR-Football-Dataset.csv {'Vasco Da Gama RJ': 419}\nnovo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv {'Vasco': 552}\n","metadata":{"output":"Brasileirao_Matches.csv {'Vasco da Gama-RJ': 266}\nBrazilian_Cup_Matches.csv {'Vasco da Gama - RJ': 54}\nLibertadores_Matches.csv {'Vasco': 6}\nBR-Football-Dataset.csv {'Vasco Da Gama RJ': 419}\nnovo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv {'Vasco': 552}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nfor path, cols in [\n    (\"data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv\", [\"home_team\",\"away_team\"]),\n    (\"data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\", [\"home_team\",\"away_team\"]),\n    (\"data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv\", [\"home_team\",\"away_team\"]),\n    (\"data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv\", [\"home\",\"away\"]),\n    (\"data/kaggle/novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\", [\"Equipe_mandante\",\"Equipe_visitante\"]),\n]:\n    c = Counter()\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(f):\n            for col in cols:\n                v = row[col].strip()\n                if \"vasco\" in v.lower():\n                    c[v] += 1\n    print(path.split(\"/\")[-1], dict(c))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788204530712,"end":1788204530715}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting changes from the display flip:\n- \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" still (brf name has no \"-\": \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" — it's space-separated! `simple` check only looks for \"-\" and \"(\" → \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" counts as simple!). And \"Vasco da Gama\" (novo, also simple) vs \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" (brf): count — brf has more? Both simple → count decides → brf wins. Hmm. And now \"Botafogo RJ\" instead of \"Botafogo-RJ\".\n- display(\"vasco da gama\") → \"vasco da gama\"?! lowercase! There must be a lowercase display \"vasco da gama\" in the data — the brf file had 'tuntum EC' lowercase... and maybe some rows have lowercase team names. \"vasco da gama\" lowercase display won because... it's simple + maybe high count? Which file has lowercase \"vasco da gama\"? Let me check. If a file has many lowercase rows... Let me find it.\n\nAlso 2020 relegated now: ['Vasco Da Gama RJ', 'Goiás', 'Coritiba', 'Botafogo RJ'] — my test expects {'Vasco Da Gama RJ', 'Goiás', 'Coritiba', 'Botafogo-RJ'} → update to \"Botafogo RJ\".\n\nLet me check where the lowercase \"vasco da gama\" comes from and refine the display scoring.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0594bbbbb0018ho4P4bcpyGlq3","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","messageID":"msg_0594b8c69001DbKxJcmM3ZtvwH"}}
