successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -58,10 +58,10 @@\n     \"santa catarina\": \"SC\", \"sao paulo\": \"SP\", \"sergipe\": \"SE\", \"tocantins\": \"TO\",\n }\n \n NOISE_TOKENS = {\n-    \"aa\", \"ac\", \"ad\", \"ae\", \"ca\", \"ce\", \"clube\", \"club\", \"cs\", \"da\", \"de\",\n-    \"do\", \"dos\", \"das\", \"e\", \"ec\", \"esporte\", \"fc\", \"ge\", \"sc\",\n+    \"aa\", \"ac\", \"ad\", \"ae\", \"ca\", \"ce\", \"clube\", \"club\", \"cs\", \"ec\", \"fc\",\n+    \"ge\", \"sc\",\n }\n \n ALIASES = {\n     \"america mineiro\": \"america-mg\",\n@@ -75,9 +75,10 @@\n     \"ceara sporting\": \"ceara\",\n     \"cs alagoano\": \"csa\",\n     \"libertad\": \"libertad-par\",\n     \"ponte pretta\": \"ponte preta\",\n-    \"sport club recife\": \"sport\",\n+    \"sport club do recife\": \"sport\",\n+    \"sport do recife\": \"sport\",\n     \"sport recife\": \"sport\",\n     \"vasco\": \"vasco da gama\",\n }\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -58,10 +58,10 @@\n     \"santa catarina\": \"SC\", \"sao paulo\": \"SP\", \"sergipe\": \"SE\", \"tocantins\": \"TO\",\n }\n \n NOISE_TOKENS = {\n-    \"aa\", \"ac\", \"ad\", \"ae\", \"ca\", \"ce\", \"clube\", \"club\", \"cs\", \"da\", \"de\",\n-    \"do\", \"dos\", \"das\", \"e\", \"ec\", \"esporte\", \"fc\", \"ge\", \"sc\",\n+    \"aa\", \"ac\", \"ad\", \"ae\", \"ca\", \"ce\", \"clube\", \"club\", \"cs\", \"ec\", \"fc\",\n+    \"ge\", \"sc\",\n }\n \n ALIASES = {\n     \"america mineiro\": \"america-mg\",\n@@ -75,9 +75,10 @@\n     \"ceara sporting\": \"ceara\",\n     \"cs alagoano\": \"csa\",\n     \"libertad\": \"libertad-par\",\n     \"ponte pretta\": \"ponte preta\",\n-    \"sport club recife\": \"sport\",\n+    \"sport club do recife\": \"sport\",\n+    \"sport do recife\": \"sport\",\n     \"sport recife\": \"sport\",\n     \"vasco\": \"vasco da gama\",\n }\n \n","additions":4,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788204596832,"end":1788204596834}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Found the real bug: `parse_team_name(\"Vasco da Gama-RJ\")` → tokens [vasco, da, gama, rj] → UF strip → [vasco, da, gama] → noise removal removes \"da\" → bare = \"vasco gama\" (NOT \"vasco da gama\"!). But `canonical(\"Vasco\")` → alias \"vasco\" → \"vasco da gama\" — a key that doesn't match the real key \"vasco gama\"!\n\nTwo problems:\n1. Removing \"da/dos/das/de\" from names corrupts multi-word names: \"Vasco da Gama\" → \"vasco gama\". Also \"Bahia de Feira\" → \"bahia feira\", \"Duque de Caxias\" → \"duque caxias\", \"Estudiantes de Mérida\" → \"estudiantes merida\". These intra-name connectors are part of club names!\n2. My ALIASES targets use \"vasco da gama\" (with \"da\") but actual key is \"vasco gama\" (without).\n\nFix decision: STOP removing connector words (do/da/de/dos/das/e) from bare names. Why did I remove them? For \"Sport Club do Recife\" → \"sport recife\". But those cases are handled by ALIASES anyway. Keeping connectors: \"Sport Club do Recife\" → bare \"sport club do recife\" → noise removes \"club\" → \"sport do recife\" — then alias \"sport do recife\"? Update alias. Coritiba \"SC Coritiba\"? Fine.\n\nLet me remove connectors from NOISE_TOKENS but KEEP \"clube/club/fc/ec/ac/sc/aa/ae/ad/ge/ca/ce/cs\". Then:\n- \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" → \"vasco da gama\" ✓\n- \"Sport Club do Recife\" → tokens [sport, club, do, recife] → remove \"club\" → \"sport do recife\" → alias \"sport do recife\" → \"sport\" (update alias key from \"sport recife\")\n- \"Sport Recife\" (brf) → \"sport recife\" → alias \"sport recife\" → \"sport\" (keep)\n- \"Clube de Regatas do Flamengo\" → \"clube regatas do flamengo\" — hmm \"clube\" removed → \"regatas do flamengo\" — subset match via tokens {regatas, do, flamengo}: key \"flamengo-rj\" bare \"flamengo\" tokens {flamengo} ⊆ {regatas, do, flamengo} ✓ resolves! OK.\n- \"Duque De Caxias RJ\" (brf) → uf RJ → \"duque de caxias\" ✓ nice.\n- \"Sao Jose - POA\" → \"sao jose poa\" ✓ same as before.\n- \"4 de Julho EC\" → remove ec → \"4 de julho\" ✓ (was \"4 julho\" before — cosmetic).\n- \"Independiente del Valle\" → \"independiente del valle\" ✓ (\"del\" wasn't noise anyway).\n- \"Ponte Pretta\" alias → \"ponte preta\" ✓ unchanged.\n- What about FIFA \"Atlético Paranaense\"? bare \"atletico paranaense\" ✓ alias.\n- novo \"Atlético-PR\" → (\"atletico\", PR) ✓.\n- Derby key \"vasco da gama\" ✓ now consistent!\n\nAlso update ALIASES: \"sport club do recife\" → after noise removal the parse gives \"sport do recife\" — add both \"sport do recife\" and \"sport recife\" → \"sport\". Also \"ceara sporting club\" → remove \"club\" → \"ceara sporting\" ✓ alias exists.\n\nAlso NOISE \"e\" removal: \"Sampaio Correa\"? no \"e\". \"Treze\"? \"Ferroviario\"? There might be clubs with standalone \"e\"... \"Mineros de Guaiana\"? Keep \"e\" out of noise? \"Racing e Tenis\"? Unlikely. I'll remove \"e\" from noise too (keep it in names). Actually \"e\" as noise was for cases like \"Clube Atlético e Recreativo\"? Rare. Remove \"e\" from NOISE set as well — safer for name integrity.\n\nWait — but removing \"do/da/de\" changes MANY bare names (e.g. brf \"Duque De Caxias RJ\" etc.) — fine, internal consistency maintained since all files get same treatment.\n\nOne more check: \"EC Bahia\" → \"bahia\" ✓; \"bahia de feira\" → \"bahia de feira\" distinct ✓ good.\n\nAlso the ALIAS value \"vasco da gama\" now equals the actual state-computed key (\"vasco da gama\" from bare + RJ stripped) ✓ consistent.\n\nAnd what about ALIASES \"america mineiro\" etc. — unaffected.\n\nNow also the display issue: after this fix, key \"vasco da gama\" states: bra (\"vasco da gama\", RJ) 266, brf 419, cup 54 → display picks \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" (simple, most count). novo \"Vasco\" (552, state (\"vasco\", RJ)) — bare \"vasco\" single uf → key \"vasco\" — a SEPARATE registry entry with 552 count! Matches use canonical → alias → all \"vasco da gama\" ✓ matches consistent. But registry has phantom \"vasco\" entry with count 552 and display \"Vasco\". Impact: list_teams shows extra \"vasco\" team (display Vasco, 558 count — hmm where did 558 come from? 552 novo + 6 lib). resolve(\"Vasco\") → alias checked FIRST → \"vasco da gama\" ✓ good. But `_candidates_for_bare` in ambiguity paths might surface \"vasco\"... e.g. resolve(\"Vasco da Gama\") → parse → bare \"vasco da gama\" no uf → alias? \"vasco da gama\" not in ALIASES (only \"vasco\") → is_known(\"vasco da gama\")? NO (not in key_counts since displays went under... wait no — \"vasco da gama\" IS in key_counts now post-fix). Hmm pre-fix it wasn't; post-fix it will be ✓.\n\nBut phantom \"vasco\" entry remains in key_counts (558) — alias targets aren't merged. Better: at finalize, states whose bare hits an ALIAS should map to the alias target! I.e., finalize should apply aliases too: for each state, check alias candidates (bare, bare-uf) → if alias exists → key = alias target. That merges novo \"Vasco\" displays and counts INTO \"vasco da gama\" — display selection would then see \"Vasco\" (552, simple) vs \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" (419, simple) vs \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" (266) → simple+count → \"Vasco\" ✓ (display \"Vasco\" — nice). And key_counts merges to one entry ✓. phantom gone.\n\nImplement in finalize: when assigning _key_of_state[state], first check alias:\n```python\ndef _alias_for_state(self, name, uf):\n    for alias_key in ([f\"{name}-{uf.lower()}\"] if uf else []) + [name]:\n        if alias_key in ALIASES: return ALIASES[alias_key]\n    return None\n```\nIn the state loop: alias_key = self._alias_for_state(name, uf); if alias_key: key_of_state[state] = alias_key; continue.\n\nSimilarly in canonical() the alias is already checked first ✓ consistent.\n\nNote alias check must ALSO respect country? e.g. alias for foreign states — skip, fine.\n\nThis also fixes \"athletico-pr\" alias merging with (\"athletico\", PR) state ✓ (already worked since alias is checked in canonical, but now registry counts merge too).\n\nAlso — \"libertad\" alias → \"libertad-par\": states (\"libertad\", None, None) bare → alias → \"libertad-par\" ✓ and (\"libertad\", None, \"PAR\") → country → \"libertad-par\" ✓ merged.\n\nNow update NOISE_TOKENS (remove do/da/de/dos/das/e) and ALIASES (add \"sport do recife\"), and finalize alias merging. Then rerun. Also the sample-questions/relegated-2020 expectations need updating after display changes (Vasco display becomes \"Vasco\"?? display merge: \"Vasco\" 552 vs \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" 419 vs \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" 266 vs \"Vasco da Gama - RJ\" 54 → simple: all except \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" and \"Vasco da Gama - RJ\" (both have \"-\")... \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" no hyphen ✓ simple. \"Vasco\" simple. count: \"Vasco\" 552 → wins → display \"Vasco\" ✓ NICE.\nBotafogo: displays for botafogo-rj: \"Botafogo-RJ\" (bra), \"Botafogo\" (lib/cup?), \"Botafogo RJ\" (brf), \"Botafogo\" (novo, 552?) — novo bare \"Botafogo\"? novo has \"Botafogo-RJ\"? earlier novo sample: \"São Paulo Botafogo-RJ\" — away \"Botafogo-RJ\" WITH suffix... novo naming is inconsistent. Anyway display likely \"Botafogo\" (novo count). Relegated 2020 → [\"Vasco\", \"Goiás\", \"Coritiba\", \"Botafogo\"]. Let me just run and see actual values, then update the test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0594cbe53001cBdVWmPsj4RfdN","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","messageID":"msg_0594c184c001r4wOzk2uLBNPMC"}}
