020(payload):\n     assert set(payload[\"result\"][\"relegated\"]) == {\n-        \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\", \"Goiás\", \"Coritiba\", \"Botafogo-RJ\",\n+        \"Vasco\", \"Goiás\", \"Coritiba\", \"Botafogo RJ\",\n     }\n \n \n def check_avg_goals(payload):\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"tests/test_sample_questions.py","time":{"start":1788204649793,"end":1788204649794}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Vasco now resolves to a single key with display \"Vasco\" ✓. But two issues:\n\n1. `display sport: \"Sport Recife\"` — the alias merges novo's bare \"Sport\"? novo \"Sport\" + UF PE → state (\"sport\", PE) → alias? \"sport-pe\" not in ALIASES, \"sport\" not in ALIASES (only \"sport recife\"/\"sport do recife\" are KEYS of the alias dict, not values)... wait no: the alias dict maps \"sport recife\"→\"sport\". So state (\"sport\", PE) has no alias → bare \"sport\" single uf {PE} → key \"sport\" ✓. Display for \"sport\": displays include \"Sport-PE\" (bra), \"Sport\" (novo 552?), \"Sport Recife\" (brf ~??), \"Sport Club do Recife\"? no that's FIFA. Simple names: \"Sport\" (novo), \"Sport Recife\" (brf) → count: novo Sport ~330? brf \"Sport Recife\" Serie A/B/C 2014-2023: Sport Serie A 2014-2023? ~6 seasons... Serie B? no — Sport mostly Serie A: ~7×38=266. Hmm \"Sport Recife\" beat \"Sport\"?? That means brf count > novo count. novo \"Sport\" with PE: Sport in Serie A 2003-2019 every season? Sport was in Serie A 2003? Sport relegated 2003?... Actually Sport was in Série A most of 2003-2019 except 2004? Hmm — whatever the counts say. \"Sport Recife\" as display is acceptable (it IS a common name for the club). Fine.\n\n2. `relegated 2020: ['Vasco', 'Goiás', 'Coritiba', 'Botafogo RJ']` — \"Botafogo RJ\" display (brf) beat \"Botafogo\" (novo). Both simple; brf count 419+ > novo Botafogo bare count? novo away \"Botafogo-RJ\" (with hyphen!) and home \"Botafogo\"? Actually novo naming shown earlier: home \"São Paulo\" (no suffix), away \"Botafogo-RJ\" (with suffix) — so novo mostly uses \"Botafogo-RJ\" (hyphenated). Bare \"Botafogo\" from lib (6?) only. So \"Botafogo RJ\" (brf, simple, 419) wins over \"Botafogo-RJ\" (bra, hyphenated, 266+novo). OK — \"Botafogo RJ\" is fine.\n\nUpdate test expectation for relegated 2020: {\"Vasco\", \"Goiás\", \"Coritiba\", \"Botafogo RJ\"}.\n\nAlso — sample test check_relegated_2020 currently expects \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" and \"Botafogo-RJ\". Update.\n\nAlso the mcp test asserting club_key \"santos-sp\" ✓ unaffected. The player test `then_club_players` uses resolve ✓.\n\nAlso — check \"santos-sp\" display? \"Santos\" probably ✓. Run full suite now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0594d8d36001Rl9hMtOjHCynbG","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","messageID":"msg_0594d4c5b001XW51hFV4vrfCkb"}}
