if m.date and m.date >= date_from_parsed]\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/service.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/service.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/service.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-e6k_mc30/retort-9f7589d26ec0/brazilian_soccer_mcp/service.py\n@@ -426,12 +426,13 @@\n     pool = self._pool(competition, season)\n if team_key:\n     pool = [m for m in pool if m.involves(team_key)]\n if opponent_key:\n-    pool = [\n-        m for m in pool\n-        if m.involves_pair(team_key or opponent_key, opponent_key)\n-    ]\n+    if team_key:\n+        pool = [m for m in pool\n+                if m.involves_pair(team_key, opponent_key)]\n+    else:\n+        pool = [m for m in pool if m.involves(opponent_key)]\n date_from_parsed = self._as_date(date_from)\n date_to_parsed = self._as_date(date_to)\n if date_from_parsed:\n     pool = [m for m in pool if m.date and m.date >= date_from_parsed]\n","additions":5,"deletions":4},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/service.py","time":{"start":1788204770468,"end":1788204770470}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All 108 tests pass. The warnings are from pytest-bdd's compat with pytest 9 — deprecation warnings, not errors. I could filter them in pytest.ini to keep output clean.\n\nRemaining work:\n1. Verify `run_server.py` actually runs (stdio server smoke test — spawn it and speak MCP over stdin? A quick check: import + initialize handshake via a script).\n2. Check performance criteria: simple lookups < 2s, aggregates < 5s (load 0.9s + queries ~ms ✓; add a perf test to document it).\n3. Update README.md describing what was done.\n4. Coverage: maybe run coverage to see if any big gaps — not required, but let me check the service code paths are all covered reasonably.\n5. Double check a couple of edge behaviors: `search_matches` with opponent but no team; `league_statistics` with source; `list_teams` query; `standings` Serie B (has standings from brf! Serie B is a league ✓ — check it works).\n6. Filter the pytest-bdd deprecation warnings in pytest.ini for clean output.\n7. Also verify the server starts via `python run_server.py` — quick handshake test over stdio using the mcp stdio client.\n\nLet me also add a performance test to the suite (spec: simple < 2s, aggregate < 5s).\n\nAlso — one thing to double-check: `standings(\"Serie B\", 2022)` — brf Serie B 2022, standings computed. And `search_matches(opponent=...)` without team — pool = _pool(None, None) = all resolved; opponent filter involves_pair(team_key or opponent_key, opponent_key) — team_key None → involves_pair(opponent_key, opponent_key) → {home,away} == {opponent} — never true (set of 2 ≠ set of 1)! Bug: opponent without team returns nothing. Hmm — should opponent alone mean \"all matches involving X\"? Logically yes. Let me handle: if opponent and not team → treat like team filter on opponent_key. Fix in search_matches:\n\n```python\nif team_key:\n    pool = [m for m in pool if m.involves(team_key)]\nif opponent_key:\n    if team_key:\n        pool = [m for m in pool if m.involves_pair(team_key, opponent_key)]\n    else:\n        pool = [m for m in pool if m.involves(opponent_key)]\n```\n\nLet me implement + test. Also the involves_pair(team_key or opponent_key, opponent_key) weirdness goes away.\n\nAlso check `_pool(competition, season)` when called from search with team set: pool = _pool(competition, season) — comp string None → fine.\n\nAlso verify list_teams works with query.\n\nLet me fix the opponent-only case and run a final broader smoke.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0594f64940018Mc0vdVfrFZ2VB","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","messageID