{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788204822132,"sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_e27e5a5929ad44a5af6c2127","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF' >> /dev/null\n# placeholder to keep bash tool output clean\nEOF"},"output":"(no output)","metadata":{"output":"(no output)","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python - <<'EOF' >> /dev/null\n# placeholder to keep bash tool output clean\nEOF","time":{"start":1788204822101,"end":1788204822131}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The stdio server works end-to-end with real subprocess transport. Now final steps:\n\n1. Update README.md to describe what was done.\n2. Run the full suite one more time + maybe with coverage to confirm.\n3. Also quickly verify the extended stats appear in match dicts (brf corners etc.) and that `search_matches` exposes a \"corner statistics\" story — spec mentions extended stats dataset must be queryable ✓ (test_loaders covers stats loading; test via source param works).\n\nAlso — should I add a tool-level example of usage in README (Claude Desktop config)? Good idea.\n\nLet me also double check there are no leftover issues:\n- `_stage_filter` handles stage like \"Round 5\" for cup ✓\n- `competition_info` for a specific comp returns source_labels ✓\n\nOne more check — the spec's cross-file query criterion: \"Cross-file queries work (e.g., player + match data)\". The players_by_club + team queries cross files. Also team_competitions crosses match files. I have a test? test_player_queries players_by_club asserts Brazilian clubs ✓ crosses FIFA + match files. Good enough, but let me add one explicit cross-file test: resolve a FIFA club (e.g. \"Santos\") → team_stats shows match record (match files) AND search_players shows squad (FIFA file). Add to test_sample_questions? It's essentially covered by \"Which players play for Santos?\" + team_stats tests. I'll add one explicit test in test_sample_questions: \"Cross-file: Santos squad and record\" — actually the 26 questions already cover this implicitly. Let me add ONE explicit cross-file test in test_team_queries as a plain (non-BDD) test at the end.\n\nThen README. Also add .gitignore? There's a venv dir and logs — the repo has _agent_stdout.log etc. Not my concern; leave.\n\nAlso — the \"run tests\" command convention: document `./venv/bin/python -m pytest` or `pip install -r requirements.txt && pytest` in README.\n\nLet me write the README and add the cross-file test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059502e52001K6BtCe3C7mM4wb","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","messageID":"msg_0594ff428001m7rw56FskX8Az7"}}
