{"type":"text","timestamp":1788204911860,"sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","part":{"id":"prt_0595179c9001UXcyPPmZxNKc4x","messageID":"msg_059516079001f2nt2j7llJV4tM","sessionID":"ses_fa6cfe050ffe51wxe0DFh4LAA3","type":"text","text":"Done. Implemented the Brazilian Soccer MCP server per TASK.md, all in Python:\n\n**Implementation** (`brazilian_soccer_mcp/` + `run_server.py`)\n- `normalize.py` — team-name canonicalization across all datasets (\"Palmeiras-SP\"/\"Palmeiras\"/\"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"/\"Atletico Mineiro\"/\"Athletico\", state suffixes, country codes like \"Nacional-URU\", accents) plus multi-format date/int parsing\n- `loaders.py` — loaders for all 6 CSVs (~24k matches, 18k players)\n- `service.py` — query engine: match search, head-to-head, team stats, computed standings, derbies, biggest wins, league statistics, best home/away records, player queries. Overlapping sources are deduplicated via per-(competition, season) source priority; the `source` parameter reaches the extended corner/shot/attack stats\n- `server.py` — MCP server (15 tools, official `mcp` SDK, stdio transport); verified end-to-end over both in-memory and real stdio transports\n\n**Tests** — 116 passing: BDD Gherkin features (`tests/features/*.feature` + pytest-bdd steps), unit tests for normalization, loader tests for all 6 files, in-process MCP protocol tests, performance tests (spec budgets: <2s lookups, <5s aggregates), cross-file join tests, and 26 end-to-end sample questions from the spec (2019 standings compute exactly Flamengo 90 pts, 28W-6D-4L; 2018/2020/2021 champions and relegations all match history).\n\n**Caveats documented in README**: the FIFA dataset lacks licensed squads for clubs like Flamengo/Corinthians (returns empty gracefully), and some late-2022 scores are missing in the data.","time":{"start":1788204906953,"end":1788204911856}}}
